.TH PGN-ECO 1
.SH NAME
pgn-eco \- check and classify ECO opening codes in PGN files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
pgn-eco [OPTIONS] \-\-check INPUT...
pgn-eco [OPTIONS] \-\-output FILE INPUT...
pgn-eco [OPTIONS] \-\-output-dir DIR INPUT...
pgn-eco [OPTIONS] \-\-in-place INPUT...
pgn-eco \-\-update-books
pgn-eco [\-\-help | \-h]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
PGN (Portable Game Notation) is a text format for chess games. ECO
(Encyclopaedia of Chess Openings) codes label a game's opening, for example
.B B32.
.PP
.B pgn-eco
reads one or more PGN files and compares their opening tags with an opening
book. It can check existing tags, write classified games to one combined
file, write one file per input, or replace input files in place. Choose
exactly one operating mode: \fB\-\-check\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR,
\fB\-\-output-dir\fR, or \fB\-\-in-place\fR. The input files are processed
in the order given.
.PP
Without \fB\-\-fill-missing\fR, a writing mode recalculates each game's ECO
tag when a unique classification is available. With \fB\-\-fill-missing\fR,
missing tags and one unsupported ECO value can be filled when classification
is unique. Supported ECO3 and ECO4 tags, and games with duplicate ECO tags,
are preserved in fill mode. Not every game can be classified.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check several files:
.nf
pgn-eco --check games-*.pgn
.fi
.TP
Write several inputs to one new file:
.nf
pgn-eco --output combined.pgn games-2024.pgn games-2025.pgn
.fi
.TP
Write PGN to standard output:
.nf
pgn-eco --output - games.pgn | wc -c
.fi
.TP
Write one output file per input. The directory must already exist:
.nf
pgn-eco --output-dir classified games-2024.pgn games-2025.pgn
.fi
.TP
Fill missing tags in new output files:
.nf
pgn-eco --fill-missing --output-dir completed games-2024.pgn games-2025.pgn
.fi
.TP
Replace each input separately after successful processing:
.nf
pgn-eco --in-place games-2024.pgn games-2025.pgn
.fi
.TP
Force sequential processing:
.nf
pgn-eco --threads 1 --output result.pgn games.pgn
.fi
.SH OPERATING MODES
.TP
.B \-\-check INPUT...
Read and check all input files without writing classified PGN. The summary
and report options cover all processed games. A difference or unresolved
game gives status 1; it does not stop checks of later files. A processing or
I/O error stops the command and takes precedence, giving status 2. With more
than one input, per-game reports include the source filename.
.TP
.B \-\-output FILE INPUT...
Write all input games, in order, to one new output file. The inputs are not
changed. Empty inputs add no bytes. A line break is added at a file boundary
only when the preceding content has no trailing line break and the next
content has no leading line break. A temporary file is written beside the
destination and is published only after all inputs succeed. The destination
must not exist. Ordinary permission bits are the intersection of the input
files' permission bits.
.TP
.B \-\-output-dir DIR INPUT...
Write one new file per input in the existing directory DIR. The output name
is the input's basename; directory paths are not copied and names are not
changed. The directory is not created automatically. Basename collisions
and any existing destination (including a symbolic or dangling link) are
rejected before processing starts. Each file is staged in DIR and published
without replacing an existing entry. Each output keeps the ordinary
permission bits of its corresponding input.
.TP
.B \-\-in-place INPUT...
Process and atomically replace each input separately. A file is replaced
only after its complete output has been written and checked. Symbolic links,
hard-linked files, repeated paths, and aliases to the active ECO book are
rejected. File ownership and permissions are preserved when possible; if
they cannot be preserved, the file is left unchanged and the operation fails.
.PP
The multi-file \fB\-\-output-dir\fR and \fB\-\-in-place\fR modes are not
transactions across the entire input list. If a later file fails, previously
completed files remain complete. A combined \fB\-\-output\fR file is
published only after every input has succeeded.
.PP
The output path must be explicit. Existing file destinations are never
silently overwritten. \fB\-\-output -\fR writes PGN to standard output and
does not create a temporary file. Reports and diagnostics go to standard
error in this mode. Standard output cannot be rolled back after an error.
Use \fB\-\-output ./-\fR to create a file literally named \fB-\fR. Use
\fB\-\-\fR before an input filename that starts with a hyphen.
.PP
New file outputs preserve the ordinary permission bits of their source. For
one combined output, the permission bits common to all inputs are used. The
process creates output files with its normal ownership and group rules; it
does not copy input ownership. Special permission bits are not copied.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fill-missing
Use fill mode with \fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-\-output-dir\fR, or
\fB\-\-in-place\fR. It is not an operating mode by itself. An absent ECO tag
or one unsupported value can be replaced when there is a unique result.
Supported ECO3/ECO4 tags and duplicate tag groups remain byte-for-byte
unchanged. Without this option, output modes update existing tags and can
collapse duplicate tags when a unique result is found.
.TP
.B \-\-mode 3 | 4
Select three-character ECO3 or four-character Scid-style ECO4 classification.
Mode 3 is the default and uses the Lichess book; mode 4 uses the Scid book.
For example, mode 4 can calculate a code such as
.BR A41e .
.TP
.B \-\-eco-book FILE
Use only the specified opening book. Supported formats include Lichess TSV,
Scid .eco, Caissabase Scid export, and pgn-extract eco.pgn. Without this
option, the configured or installed default is used.
.TP
.B \-\-threads N
Set the maximum number of worker threads. If omitted or set to 0, the program
uses input sizes and the number of input files to decide whether workers are
useful, then limits them to available logical CPUs. On Linux it considers CPU
affinity and common cgroup CPU quotas. Use 1 to force sequential processing.
An explicit value of 2 or more enables workers up to that limit. The pool is
started only when the first game needs classification. Results remain in
input order.
.TP
.B \-\-limit N
Check at most N complete games across the entire ordered input list. N must
be a positive decimal integer. This option is valid only with
.BR \-\-check .
Once the global limit is reached, the rest of the current file and later
files are not read. This option cannot produce a truncated replacement file.
.TP
.B \-\-details
For \fB\-\-check\fR, show totals by ECO code and common code changes.
.TP
.B \-\-per-game
For \fB\-\-check\fR, print a compact result for each game. For multiple
inputs, each line identifies its input file and game number within that file.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
For \fB\-\-check\fR, show reference positions, FEN, match depth, candidates,
and history-selection details.
.TP
.B \-\-update-books
Download, check, and install the standard Lichess three-character book and
the Scid four-character book for offline use. Requires an internet
connection, curl, and sha256sum. Each book is verified before activation.
If the Scid update fails after Lichess has been installed, the command reports
the partial completion and keeps the previous Scid book. This command accepts
no other options or input files.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Print command usage.
.PP
.BR \-\-details ,
.BR \-\-per-game ,
and
.B \-\-debug
are mutually exclusive and apply only to \fB\-\-check\fR.
.SH ECO TAGS
A tag is missing only when no \fBECO\fR tag is present. An empty value,
.BR ? ,
or a value such as
.B D37/22
has unsupported notation. pgn-eco does not shorten slash values. ECO3 values
(A00 to E99) and supported ECO4 values (such as A41e) are syntactically
valid in either mode. The selected mode determines the code that is
calculated. A prefix-compatible result confirms only the first three
characters, not the fourth character.
.SH OPENING BOOKS
.SS Standard three-character book
Run
.B "pgn-eco --update-books"
once to install the Lichess ECO3 book and the Scid ECO4 book. Mode 3 uses
Lichess by default; mode 4 uses Scid by default. Classification with an
installed book works offline.
.SS Four-character Scid book
To use a local Scid book, pass its path and select mode 4:
.nf
pgn-eco --mode 4 --eco-book /path/to/scid.eco --check games.pgn
.fi
The updater obtains the original Scid book at a pinned revision from
.I https://github.com/benini/scid/ .
The file keeps its copyright header. The repository's COPYING file states
that Scid files other than listed third-party contributions use GPL version
2; scid.eco is not listed as an exclusion. pgn-eco does not bundle this book.
.PP
If \fB\-\-eco-book FILE\fR is given, only that book is used. Otherwise a
non-empty \fBPGN_ECO_BOOK\fR selects the default, followed by the installed
search locations. Books can differ in coverage and code choices.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Processing succeeded. For \fB\-\-check\fR, no differences or unresolved
findings were found.
.TP
.B 1
\fB\-\-check\fR found a difference or another unresolved finding. This is
not a processing error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments, input/output failure, invalid book, or other processing
error. For multiple check inputs, a processing error takes precedence over
ordinary classification differences.
.SH SAFETY
Input files are read-only except when \fB\-\-in-place\fR is explicitly
selected. New output files are never allowed to replace an existing path.
The program validates input and destination paths before classification and
checks them again during file operations. It uses temporary files in the
destination directory and removes them on failure. PGN bytes outside ECO tag
lines that are deliberately changed are preserved.
.PP
In-place mode stages a replacement on the same filesystem, checks writes,
flush and close, then replaces one input atomically. It rejects symlinks,
hard links and repeated aliases rather than changing their link behaviour.
For multiple files, each replacement is separate; earlier completed files
are not rolled back if a later file fails.
.SH LIMITATIONS
pgn-eco is an opening classifier, not a complete chess-game validator. It
checks relevant legal moves near the start of the main line, up to the book
horizon (at most 40 half-moves). It skips move legality checks inside RAVs
(parenthesized variations) and after the opening horizon. It still checks PGN
structure needed for safe record handling. Invalid moves in the relevant
opening can prevent classification. Some positions are ambiguous or absent
from the selected book.
.PP
Only standard chess is supported. A book may use different labels or cover
different lines from another book.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PGN_ECO_BOOK
Default book path when \fB\-\-eco-book\fR is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the per-user Lichess book in mode 3 and Scid book in mode
4 when it is an absolute path.
.TP
.B PGN_ECO_TIMING
Set to 1 to print phase timings and worker-pool information to standard
error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/pgn-eco/lichess-openings.tsv
Per-user three-character Lichess book when XDG_DATA_HOME is absolute.
.TP
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/pgn-eco/scid.eco
Per-user four-character Scid book when XDG_DATA_HOME is absolute.
.TP
.B $HOME/.local/share/pgn-eco/lichess-openings.tsv
Fallback per-user three-character Lichess book location.
.TP
.B $HOME/.local/share/pgn-eco/scid.eco
Fallback per-user four-character Scid book location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pgn-extract (1)
